# sphere_clear.cam — the revolve-boss Clear (DECISIONS.md "roughing a convex
# revolve…", slice 1). The first fixture in this project whose stock actually
# CONTAINS its part: every other convex-revolve fixture datums the feature at
# the stock top so the dome stands in air, because until this op existed a
# containing stock made the program a HARD ERROR — check_moves had no earlier
# op to credit with opening the material the finish pass enters.
#
# T1 roughs the moat around the buried dome in Z levels down to the equator
# plane, leaving a 0.5mm allowance; T9 finishes the dome out of what T1 opened.
#
# What this fixture claims, exactly: the program BUILDS and is SILENT. The
# containment lint is quiet (the part fits the stock), check_moves passes on
# both ops, the swept-tube ceiling accounts for the rim area the ball sweeps
# beside the equator (DECISIONS.md "rim-area accounting…", slices 0-1), and
# T9's apex entry — a plunge through the residual cap its own rough left,
# category 3 by charter — is licensed by the derived pairing (fork 3A): a
# finish behind its own rough cuts only what it declares on the way in.
#
# What is deliberately NOT machined: the stock outside the moat. Nothing
# declares that it should go — the moat is one tool diameter past the rim,
# which is the width a tool must sweep to reach an edge at all — so the dome
# comes out standing on a pedestal. A program that wants the whole block down
# says so with a Floor.
#
# rapid_z clears the stock TOP (z=22), not z=0: this is the first fixture whose
# stock top is not the origin, and a rapid at 5 would cross the stock.
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 25
clearance_z 40
spindle 4000

# The stock stands 2mm proud of the dome's apex (z=20) and reaches 25mm below
# its equator plane.
stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=47, x=0, y=0, z=22)

tool T1 Endmill(dia=12.0)
tool T9 Ballmill(dia=6.0)

# Sphere centre (equator plane) at z=0; the machinable dome rises to z=20.
feature TopDome Sphere(dia=40, x=50, y=40, z=0)

run Clear(tool=T1, profile=TopDome, stepover=8.0, stepdown=5.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run Copy(tool=T9, surface=TopDome, stepover=3.0)
